1
00:00:01,534 --> 00:00:04,859
Fire Truck with a Phobia!

2
00:00:08,198 --> 00:00:09,141
Haha!

3
00:00:09,742 --> 00:00:10,965
Did we keep you waiting?

4
00:00:10,965 --> 00:00:13,384
An all new Milky Way special!

5
00:00:13,384 --> 00:00:15,151
We call it... The Flame Tower!

6
00:00:15,651 --> 00:00:17,637
The Flame Tower...?

7
00:00:17,637 --> 00:00:19,660
Shall we begin?

8
00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:20,568
Mhm.

9
00:00:30,388 --> 00:00:31,789
Surprise!

10
00:00:31,789 --> 00:00:34,555
Wow! This looks amazing!

11
00:00:36,122 --> 00:00:39,545
You see? Everyone loves a little bit of a performance.

12
00:00:39,545 --> 00:00:42,226
You really are the best, Dad!

13
00:00:43,411 --> 00:00:45,453
Huh? Is there a fire?

14
00:00:45,453 --> 00:00:47,155
I think it's getting closer...

15
00:00:52,167 --> 00:00:54,591
Fire! Please evacuate!

16
00:00:58,533 --> 00:00:59,939
Fire extinguished!

17
00:01:03,270 --> 00:01:05,087
Ugh...

18
00:01:07,170 --> 00:01:08,763
Aah!!

19
00:01:09,864 --> 00:01:11,914
Urgh! What kind of surprise was that?!

20
00:01:11,914 --> 00:01:14,031
Ah, no, Anna, it's not-

21
00:01:14,031 --> 00:01:15,307
Save it!

22
00:01:16,248 --> 00:01:17,966
No, Anna, wait!

23
00:01:21,462 --> 00:01:24,146
Anna, please don't go!!

24
00:01:27,646 --> 00:01:29,475
Anna...

25
00:01:29,475 --> 00:01:30,195
Jun.

26
00:01:33,350 --> 00:01:36,981
Jun. That fire truck just now was a Metal Cardbot.

27
00:01:36,981 --> 00:01:40,700
That's not important right now. Dang it!

28
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:41,825
Jun!

29
00:01:41,825 --> 00:01:43,728
What are you doing?

30
00:01:48,959 --> 00:01:52,876
Seems like similar cases have been popping up everywhere these days.

31
00:01:52,876 --> 00:01:56,584
People were having a barbeque in their yard when they were sprayed with extinguisher fluid...

32
00:01:58,496 --> 00:02:01,292
The torch at an olympic relay was put out...

33
00:02:03,203 --> 00:02:07,144
Even candles on a birthday cake were blown out by a fire truck!

34
00:02:08,473 --> 00:02:11,634
Ugh, what is going on in this city...?!

35
00:02:11,634 --> 00:02:14,068
Was it all because of that fire truck?

36
00:02:14,068 --> 00:02:15,205
Probably...

37
00:02:15,205 --> 00:02:19,877
Urgh! I'm gonna find him and make him kneel before Anna and apologize!

38
00:02:19,877 --> 00:02:22,733
You can seal them, but you mustn't reveal the Metal Cardbots.

39
00:02:22,733 --> 00:02:24,853
I know, but...

40
00:02:24,853 --> 00:02:28,191
Ugh! How do I set things straight with Anna, then?

41
00:02:28,579 --> 00:02:29,990
Phoenix Fire.

42
00:02:30,341 --> 00:02:33,413
Huh? Do you know them, Mega Ambler?

43
00:02:33,413 --> 00:02:36,271
Yes. We were part of the same rescue team.

44
00:02:36,812 --> 00:02:38,930
He used to be the bravest firefighter,

45
00:02:38,930 --> 00:02:40,924
always jumping head first into the flames.

46
00:02:40,924 --> 00:02:45,986
He received the Metal Medal, an honor awarded to only the best rescue workers on planet Machina.

47
00:02:46,485 --> 00:02:49,687
If he's such a hero, why's he playing all these pranks now?

48
00:02:49,687 --> 00:02:54,485
I don't think these are pranks. He seems to be genuinely afraid of fire.

49
00:02:54,485 --> 00:02:57,924
Afraid of fire? A rescue worker with a Metal Medal?

50
00:02:57,924 --> 00:03:01,757
I can't be certain. Not without giving him a proper counseling session.

51
00:03:01,757 --> 00:03:05,893
That cowardly fire truck... what do you think he's up to now?

52
00:03:05,893 --> 00:03:09,098
Jun, that's a smoke bomb! Don't touch it, it's not safe.

53
00:03:09,098 --> 00:03:11,193
Oh! Okay...

54
00:03:27,548 --> 00:03:28,574
Hmm...

55
00:03:30,211 --> 00:03:33,343
Confirming Metal Cardbot ID on the planet directly ahead.

56
00:03:33,343 --> 00:03:34,849
Initiating landing.

57
00:03:41,709 --> 00:03:43,477
Error in the controls!

58
00:03:45,816 --> 00:03:48,090
Oh no!

59
00:03:50,622 --> 00:03:54,204
This is bad... the controls aren't working!

60
00:03:54,204 --> 00:03:55,257
Agh!

61
00:04:02,763 --> 00:04:05,379
I had that dream again...

62
00:04:08,896 --> 00:04:11,427
Fire... is just too dangerous.

63
00:04:12,628 --> 00:04:17,257
There must be oxygen for something to catch fire.

64
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:20,447
For example, when you place a lit candle inside a jar...

65
00:04:20,447 --> 00:04:22,338
Really? Set a trap?

66
00:04:22,338 --> 00:04:25,072
Well, since Phoenix Fire can't stand fire,

67
00:04:25,072 --> 00:04:26,737
let's just make one to lure him out.

68
00:04:26,737 --> 00:04:29,961
Yeah, but a fire will bring real fire trucks as well.

69
00:04:29,961 --> 00:04:31,913
Right. That's a problem...

70
00:04:31,913 --> 00:04:34,699
Hey, you two! Pay attention!

71
00:04:34,699 --> 00:04:36,002
We're sorry!

72
00:04:36,502 --> 00:04:38,971
So, shall we begin the experiment?

73
00:04:44,718 --> 00:04:45,812
Huh?

74
00:04:48,576 --> 00:04:50,314
Is that another fire truck?

75
00:04:50,314 --> 00:04:51,673
It's him!

76
00:04:58,771 --> 00:05:00,071
Where's the fire?

77
00:05:02,372 --> 00:05:07,470
Oh my... Woah... A real fire truck... That's so cool! (FX-italic)

78
00:05:07,470 --> 00:05:08,346
Theo.

79
00:05:09,446 --> 00:05:11,238
Huh? Are you serious?

80
00:05:11,238 --> 00:05:13,584
You're the only one that can help me with this!

81
00:05:13,584 --> 00:05:16,677
Uh, okay... I'll do it!

82
00:05:23,144 --> 00:05:26,228
I'm wondering if there has been a mistake. There's no fire here-

83
00:05:26,228 --> 00:05:29,082
Fire alert! This is a fire alert!

84
00:05:29,082 --> 00:05:31,932
All students, please evacuate immediately!

85
00:05:31,932 --> 00:05:33,661
Huh? Oh no!

86
00:05:34,725 --> 00:05:37,711
There has been a fire! All students, please!

87
00:05:37,711 --> 00:05:39,810
You have to evacuate the building!

88
00:05:41,024 --> 00:05:42,096
It's the real deal?

89
00:05:42,096 --> 00:05:44,069
Let's get out of here!

90
00:05:46,683 --> 00:05:49,524
Stay calm, everyone! Please walk, don't run!

91
00:05:53,737 --> 00:05:57,074
It's okay, everyone! Don't panic! Stay calm!

92
00:05:57,927 --> 00:06:00,324
Jun, where are you going?

93
00:06:00,324 --> 00:06:03,057
I'll go check if there are others who haven't evacuated.

94
00:06:03,057 --> 00:06:05,177
Anna, please take care of our classmates.

95
00:06:05,177 --> 00:06:07,425
Alright. Be careful!

96
00:06:11,997 --> 00:06:13,334
Is that the fire?

97
00:06:16,814 --> 00:06:19,153
There's a fire! Evacuate!

98
00:06:19,778 --> 00:06:24,153
Hehe! Sorry, but it's not a real fire!

99
00:06:24,153 --> 00:06:26,326
What? You tricked me!

100
00:06:35,187 --> 00:06:37,101
Metal Breath, pickup!

101
00:06:38,858 --> 00:06:40,526
Blue Cop, setup!

102
00:07:04,961 --> 00:07:06,987
That's enough, Phoenix Fire!

103
00:07:09,810 --> 00:07:11,877
What's wrong with putting out fires?!

104
00:07:11,877 --> 00:07:14,423
Fire is proof of civilization to the people of this planet.

105
00:07:14,423 --> 00:07:16,521
You shouldn't put out just any fire.

106
00:07:16,521 --> 00:07:17,920
That doesn't concern me!

107
00:07:21,540 --> 00:07:23,701
You don't know how scary fire can be!

108
00:07:23,701 --> 00:07:26,199
All fires need to be put out!

109
00:07:47,038 --> 00:07:48,750
Blue Cop, use your Burst Shot!

110
00:07:48,750 --> 00:07:49,598
Got it!

111
00:07:50,384 --> 00:07:51,918
Burst Shot!

112
00:07:54,348 --> 00:07:57,018
Huh? F-Fire...?

113
00:07:57,117 --> 00:07:58,332
Augh!

114
00:08:04,781 --> 00:08:05,923
That's...

115
00:08:05,923 --> 00:08:08,264
That's Phoenix Fire's Metal Medal!

116
00:08:10,583 --> 00:08:15,240
Fire! Everything will go up in flames if I don't do something!

117
00:08:18,728 --> 00:08:21,752
It's covered in soot. I guess we know how he got a phobia of fire.

118
00:08:21,752 --> 00:08:24,689
Looks like it's time for the doctor to step in.

119
00:08:28,682 --> 00:08:30,158
Mega Ambler, setup!

120
00:08:33,919 --> 00:08:35,354
It's too early to take a break.

121
00:08:35,354 --> 00:08:37,870
Pick yourself up and get back to it!

122
00:08:40,570 --> 00:08:43,739
That did the trick... thanks, Mega Ambler.

123
00:08:44,363 --> 00:08:46,302
So, you're a real doctor after all.

124
00:08:46,302 --> 00:08:49,153
Now, Blue Cop will be able to help Phoenix Fire.

125
00:08:52,138 --> 00:08:53,798
Wake up, Phoenix Fire.

126
00:08:53,798 --> 00:08:56,061
You used to be a brave rescue worker!

127
00:08:56,061 --> 00:08:57,221
What do you know?!

128
00:09:00,719 --> 00:09:02,706
Blue Cop, watch out!

129
00:09:05,068 --> 00:09:09,763
Let's end it with this! Megabolt... Punch!

130
00:09:09,763 --> 00:09:11,672
Megabolt...

131
00:09:11,672 --> 00:09:13,440
Punch!

132
00:09:23,903 --> 00:09:24,826
Now!

133
00:09:25,932 --> 00:09:29,465
Metal Cardbot, Change Up!

134
00:09:47,998 --> 00:09:51,389
Phoenix Fire, sealed!

135
00:09:54,110 --> 00:09:56,538
Haha!

136
00:10:00,793 --> 00:10:02,423
Phew...

137
00:10:05,738 --> 00:10:08,706
I changed out your temperature sensor because it was burnt out.

138
00:10:08,706 --> 00:10:12,857
It might take some time to get used to the new sensor, since it was made here on Earth.

139
00:10:13,596 --> 00:10:15,822
Glad you're okay now, Phoenix Fire!

140
00:10:16,384 --> 00:10:19,302
I'm sorry for causing trouble. Let's be a good team from now on!

141
00:10:19,302 --> 00:10:20,232
The hero has returned.

142
00:10:20,232 --> 00:10:22,090
Glad to have you back.

143
00:10:22,090 --> 00:10:23,855
Hello?

144
00:10:28,129 --> 00:10:30,086
So you were here!

145
00:10:30,086 --> 00:10:32,548
Anna...?! What brings you here?

146
00:10:32,548 --> 00:10:34,937
I thought I'd thank you for what you did.

147
00:10:34,937 --> 00:10:37,278
Here, it's a piping hot apple pie!

148
00:10:37,278 --> 00:10:40,226
Wait, you mean you made this yourself?!

149
00:10:40,226 --> 00:10:43,298
Eat it while it's hot! I think it should still be...

150
00:10:43,423 --> 00:10:45,500
Hot...pie...

151
00:10:45,500 --> 00:10:48,100
I have to put it out!

152
00:10:48,100 --> 00:10:50,490
- Calm down.
- There's no fire...

153
00:10:50,490 --> 00:10:55,145
Ahhh, this is amazing! it's Anna's homemade apple pie!

154
00:10:55,145 --> 00:10:57,400
Hey Uncle Edo, can you bring us some drinks?!

155
00:10:57,400 --> 00:10:59,277
Get them yourself!

